Z||000000||85GT4ME||04-09-2001||07:50 PM||||Ok I know the rear brake clip which may be called a chatter clip which holds the pad in place is not nessary but if you don't have it you may be afraid of your pads falling out while driving.  I have no Idea where mine went but man I sure could use a new one.  I think a Junk Yard might be my best luck. I got some money in my pocket for who ever can accuire me one. Thanks in advance!||||reg||4
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-09-2001||09:36 PM||||Go to Auto Zone or another local parts store and get a hardware kit for the rear brakes. The clips ar in it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||04-10-2001||09:21 AM||||Better yet, tell me how many you need and I'll send them to you free.<P>The rebuild kit I bought for my front calipers had them even though I didn't need them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-10-2001||07:28 PM||||The anti rattle clip in the rear is also to help with pulling the pad off the rotor. That is why it goes on the piston the way it does.<P>The pad will not fall out of the car w/o the clip. It will wear the face of the piston and usually make all sorts of noise. The pad will also drag more resulting in increased wear.||||reg||1
